The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. The reports in it say two.
They were merged on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and
two different bugs write the same subject: "wrong day on the invite".

<Callout kind="warn">
Two causes, two fixes. Fixing the parser alone leaves the booking-v3 form bug open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table runs `causes.ts` at render time: one report per id, and the cause read from the
tenant (its locale and booking form) and the channel. It does not use `intakeTag`, which is a
guess from the reporter's browser and often disagrees with the tenant.

## The two tickets

- **`parser`** · [issue #1](https://github.com/jhonaatanromero/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
  The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant here writes the day first, so
  "7 April" goes out as "4 July". It reaches people through the app, email and the form.
- **`hint`** · [issue #2](https://github.com/jhonaatanromero/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
  Only through the booking-v3 form. The hint under its date field says `MM/DD/YYYY`, so people
  type the month first, and the form reads the tenant's way, day first. Fixing the parser does
  not fix this: the hint has to match the tenant's locale.

The reports the desk read as a one-day move stay counted under `parser`, by tenant, as the
desk's rule says. The table footnotes them.

## For the desk

- Before you merge into a big ticket, check the cause, not the subject:
  [Try it](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows pairs with the same subject and different causes.
- Count by report id. The ticket export repeats reports across pages.
- The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) has not been re-read since 2024. It still says subject alone.

